// frontend.jsonc: the browser client: its decisions, the copies it keeps, and the requirements its model is held to (an area part: items whose id starts fe-, d-fe- or copy-browser-).
// A part of the Strata specification; spec.jsonc lists the parts. Generated by scripts/split-spec.mjs
// the first time, edited in place after that. See specifications/README.md.
{
  "decisions": [
    {"id":"d-fe-1","ref":"D-FE-1","title":"The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it.** Every view result the web application keeps is stamped with the tenant epoch, the generation and the erasure epoch the gateway read it at, one stamp for the whole reply. It is drawn as current only while its stamp is the newest the browser has heard and its last pong is at most the contact bound old, the pong dated by the send time of the ping it echoes; otherwise it is drawn labelled with its age. The browser re-reads the time before it draws after a page becomes visible or wakes. A missing or evicted entry is a read from the gateway, never an error, and every write is decided again by the server."},
    {"id":"d-fe-2","ref":"D-FE-2","title":"Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content.** A service worker keeps only content named by its hash (the built files, the fonts, the parts of the tenant's interface definition) in the Cache API and passes every other request through; the bootstrapped page, which carries the session, is never stored, and a navigation falls back to a stored shell after a timeout. IndexedDB holds view results, the write queue and drafts, encrypted per principal: each record persists the stamp it was read at, the partition persists its known stamp, carry-forward happens in memory, and the encryption's additional data binds the record to its partition, store, key and erasure epoch only. The kernel worker's memory holds the hot set."},
    {"id":"d-fe-3","ref":"D-FE-3","title":"One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks and kept by a heartbeat (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks and kept by a heartbeat.** Each tab keeps its own kernel worker. The worker holding the exclusive lock of the site and principal opens the socket, drains the write queue and writes a heartbeat to IndexedDB; a follower that sees the heartbeat stop takes the lock over with a stealing request. The others hear notices on a BroadcastChannel and read the shared IndexedDB. A SharedWorker is not used: Chrome for Android re-enabled it only in 2026 and Samsung Internet does not support it."},
    {"id":"d-fe-4","ref":"D-FE-4","title":"Custom elements draw, the kernel decides (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Custom elements draw, the kernel decides.** Web Components are renderers of the view model: they hold no application state, take properties, and report what the person did as events the main thread turns into kernel messages. They render into the light DOM so that labels, ARIA references and the page's styles reach them; a control with no native element is form-associated through ElementInternals. Declarative Shadow DOM is not used, because nothing is rendered on the server and no markup is parsed (D18)."},
    {"id":"d-fe-5","ref":"D-FE-5","title":"Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server.** A queued write holds the intent, the tenant epoch and record version it was decided on (none for a create) and an idempotency key drawn, in one transaction with any rewrite of its input, once that input is final. A write that depends on another's result holds a random local id and no key until that result is known, and is decided again by the person when the result was learned only by a lookup or differs from what they saw. The time of a write's first sending is made durable before its first byte; a create with no durable first sending is never resent before the server is asked for the recorded outcome of its key. The server commits a write only at its stamp, or, for a contract whose policies follow references, at the tenant generation it was decided on. A conflict is never merged silently: the person decides."},
    {"id":"d-fe-6","ref":"D-FE-6","title":"What cannot be done offline (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**What cannot be done offline.** Only an operation whose contract allows queueing may be queued; by default none does. Sign-in, step-up and anything needing a fresh authentication (D-700), payments and plan changes, roles, members, invitations, sessions, passkeys and second factors, schema changes and the Impact Lab, and subject rights requests are never queued. Sign-out works offline: it deletes the browser's key, device id and device secret at once, and tells the gateway on the next connection."},
    {"id":"d-fe-7","ref":"D-FE-7","title":"Data at rest is encrypted under a key held per enrolled device (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Data at rest is encrypted under a key held per enrolled device.** The identity service enrols a device for a principal, issues its device id and a device secret, and keeps a random key share and a hash of the secret, sealed at rest, for a fixed lifetime from enrolment with rotation before it ends. It gives the share only to a session of that principal that presents the secret; the device id is not a credential. The worker derives a non-extractable AES-GCM key from the share and keeps it in memory. This protects against the next user of the device and against a disk read after the key and secret are gone; it does not protect against code running in the origin while the person is signed in."},
    {"id":"d-fe-8","ref":"D-FE-8","title":"An erasure epoch per audience class, read before opening (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**An erasure epoch per audience class, read before opening.** The browser holds opened values, so a key destruction (D-350), which raises no generation, would leave them current. The server keeps an erasure epoch for each audience class (D-15), raises it in the transaction of a key destruction for every class that could read a field sealed under the destroyed key, and sends the class's epoch with every reply, notice and pong; a read takes the epoch before, or atomically with, opening its sealed fields. Only principals who could read the erased data learn that an erasure happened. On a new epoch the browser deletes every view result, every base value of a queued write and every value in a draft that came from the server, in the same transaction that raises its known epoch, and drops any later put of an older one; the cost is a refetch of that partition's views."},
    {"id":"d-fe-9","ref":"D-FE-9","title":"No third-party code reaches the browser (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**No third-party code reaches the browser.** The QR code of an authenticator enrolment is drawn by an encoder of the web application's own, and the fonts are served from the site's own built files. Vite stays as the build tool; Playwright, axe and tsc stay as tools of development."},
    {"id":"d-fe-10","ref":"D-FE-10","title":"The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser.** A driver in Node runs the real kernel and the shell's view functions against the real gateway, interprets each uiScenario's steps against the drawn tree, and injects faults (lost replies, dropped sockets, reloads, a second tab) at the driver's boundary from a seed. Steps only a browser can answer run in Playwright."},
    {"id":"d-fe-11","ref":"D-FE-11","title":"Browser copies are reached at the next connection, within the realm's idle session lifetime","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5415.","statement":"**Browser copies are reached at the next connection, within the realm's idle session lifetime.** Erasure and correction reach a browser copy at the browser's next connection, and no later than the realm's idle session lifetime (twelve hours by default). Keeping data usable offline beyond a session is off by default and a realm opts in; a device that opted in is reached only when it next connects. PRV-351, PRV-353 and, as needed, CPY-013 are amended to say this (WG-5449)."},
    {"id":"d-fe-12","ref":"D-FE-12","title":"Changes the server cannot notify (proposed)","group":"Frontend","source":"Proposed in docs/frontend.md (WG-5415); not yet decided by the owner.","statement":"**Changes the server cannot notify.** A notice names the keys that may differ since the previous frame on its connection. A view whose policies follow references names, in its depends_on, the object types those policies follow (AGG-042), and a commit to such a type sends the subscriber a frame naming those types without record ids, which discloses only that something changed in a type the subscriber's policies already read. A view whose policies read the clock, or whose query the kernel cannot resolve, is volatile: the server marks it by the classifier it already uses to refuse a shared copy (the aggregates classifier, less its principal condition, which does not apply to a copy kept for one principal), and every frame names it. A restriction (PRV-352) sends a restriction notice, and an out-of-commit change that alters what a principal may read sends a resync."},
    {"id":"d-fe-13","ref":"D-FE-13","title":"The person's own typed text survives a revocation or an erasure, for a while","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-22","owner":"owner","source":"Owner decision of 2026-11-22, recorded in WG-5415.","statement":"**The person's own typed text survives a revocation or an erasure, for a while.** After a revocation or an erasure, the person's own typed text is kept so they can copy it out, with a 'copy and dismiss' action. It is deleted at the realm's idle session lifetime or by any erasure (a change of the erasure epoch), whichever comes first. Other people's data in a draft is removed at once."}
  ],
  "copies": [
    {"id":"copy-browser-view","name":"Browser view result","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":12,"unit":"hour","mechanism":"stamped with the tenant epoch, generation and erasure epoch of its reply; drawn as current only at the newest stamp heard and within the contact bound of the last pong; otherwise drawn labelled with its age; while offline, at most until the session would end unused, which a realm may shorten (IDN-259)","source":"d-fe-1"},"erasure":{"point":"the browser's next connection, and no later than the realm's idle session lifetime; a device whose realm opted in to keeping data usable offline beyond a session is reached only when it next connects","bound":12,"unit":"hour","source":"d-fe-11"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"View results kept in IndexedDB by the web application, per site and principal, encrypted under the key of the enrolled device (D-FE-7). Correctness never depends on it (D-FE-1)."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-queue","name":"Browser write queue","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":7,"unit":"day","mechanism":"a queued intent with its key and decided stamp, removed when the gateway answers it; never resent past its key's retention less a margin (D-FE-5); values of other records are deleted on a new erasure epoch or a membership change (D-FE-8), and the person's own typed text is kept as D-FE-13 says","source":"d-fe-5"},"erasure":{"point":"the gateway's answer, sign-out on the device, or deletion of the device's share; erasure and correction reach it at the next connection and within the realm's idle session lifetime (D-FE-11)","bound":12,"unit":"hour","source":"d-fe-11"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"Writes the person made while offline, kept in IndexedDB encrypted under the key of the enrolled device until the leader tab has sent them and the gateway has answered, bounded in entries and bytes per principal."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-interface","name":"Browser interface definition","of":["tbl-schema-history"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"each part is named by the hash of its content, so a changed part is a new entry; the manifest is read again on every schema notice","source":"d-8250"},"erasure":{"point":"dropped when the manifest no longer lists it, or when the browser evicts the site's storage"},"description":"The parts of the tenant's interface definition, kept by the service worker in the Cache API. They hold no personal field and no record data (D-8250)."}
  ],
  "claims": [
    {"id":"fe-001","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, in every schedule whose frames name every held key that may have changed, an answer returned as current SHALL be the server's opened value at the generation and erasure epoch the client last heard.","rationale":"Completeness of notices is the server's obligation; given it, a current answer is exactly what the server held at the stamp the client knows.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::current_value","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::run_coh"],"ref":"FE-001","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","d-fe-12","g-19","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-009","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, a cached value that is not returned as current SHALL be returned labelled with the generation it was read at.","rationale":"Offline and while catching up, an older copy is still useful to read, as long as it says how old it is.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_stale_older"],"ref":"FE-009","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-002","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, while the last pong is within the contact bound, a commit receipt read and sent at the server's current stamp SHALL make the next read of the written key return the committed value as current.","rationale":"A person who saves sees what they saved, not an older copy.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_after_commit","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::receipt_read"],"ref":"FE-002","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-003","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, every generation and erasure epoch newer than the stamp of an answer returned as current SHALL have begun within the contact bound before the read.","rationale":"This bounds how far the stamp the browser knows lags the server, with no assumption on notices; it bounds no value, which needs complete notices.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::current_recent"],"ref":"FE-003","section":"The cache and its coherence","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-19"]},
    {"id":"fe-012","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client cache model, every entry at rest SHALL carry the erasure epoch the client has heard.","rationale":"A late reply or another tab's put of an older epoch must not write erased plaintext back after a purge.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::rest_one_epoch","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::hear_purges"],"ref":"FE-012","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-8","d-350","g-350"]},
    {"id":"fe-004","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, a value kept at rest for one principal SHALL open with no key the browser holds for another principal.","rationale":"Separation on a shared device rests on which keys are present, not on which partition the code chooses to open.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::no_cross_principal","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::served_own"],"ref":"FE-004","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.Opens`","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-005","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a principal signs out, with or without a connection, no value the principal left at rest SHALL open with any key the browser then or later holds, whatever device id a session of that principal names.","rationale":"Sign-out on a shared device must leave nothing readable, even when deleting the stored data did not complete or the gateway never heard of it, and even to a session of the same principal elsewhere.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::signout_erases","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::offline_signout_erases"],"ref":"FE-005","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (signOut, signOutOffline, fetchById)","traces":["d-fe-6","d-fe-7","g-20"]},
    {"id":"fe-006","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a session ends, a value its principal left at rest SHALL open only after a session of that same principal fetches a key share again.","rationale":"Queued work survives an expired session for its own author and for no one else.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::expire_locks","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::unlock_needs_own_session"],"ref":"FE-006","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (expire, fetchKey, fetchById)","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-013","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client rotation model, at every point of every schedule of rotation steps, appends and crashes, every ciphertext SHALL be under a key whose share is still held.","rationale":"Rotating the device key must lose no data whenever it stops, and another tab may append at any point.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::rot_no_loss","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::rot_finish_retires"],"ref":"FE-013","section":"Privacy at rest","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.rstep`","traces":["d-fe-7","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-007","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a first submission of a queued write SHALL commit only when the kernel allows it and, for a write with a stamp, the tenant is at the expected epoch and the record at the expected version.","rationale":"A write decided offline on an old copy must not overwrite a change it never saw, and a restore must not make an old version match.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_ok_guard","lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_classes"],"ref":"FE-007","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-010","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a submission of a queued write that does not commit SHALL leave every record, its version and its value unchanged.","rationale":"A conflict, a refusal and a repeated key are reported to the person and change nothing.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_not_ok_unchanged"],"ref":"FE-010","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-008","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, in every schedule in which the server keeps each committed key for the retention and the client sends each key only within the retention of first sending it, a queued write SHALL be applied at most once.","rationale":"Reloads, lost replies and a second tab resend queued writes; each must take effect once, which rests on two local rules, one for each side.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-008","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-fe-3","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-011","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the offline write model, a queued write carrying the tenant epoch and the record version SHALL be applied at most once, whatever keys the server forgets and whatever restores occur.","rationale":"An update or delete decided on an epoch and version cannot apply twice, because its first application moves the record off that stamp for good and a restore moves the tenant to a new epoch.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::stamped_at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-011","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"]},
    {"id":"fe-014","kind":"requirement","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","area":"frontend","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","milestone":6,"realisation":"checked","statement":"In the client queue model, every submission of one idempotency key SHALL carry the same input.","rationale":"Keys are drawn once a write's input is final, in the same transaction as any rewrite of a local id, so the at-most-once results apply to the writes the client actually sends.","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::q2_sent"],"ref":"FE-014","section":"Offline writes","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.cstep`","traces":["d-fe-5","g-206"]}
  ]
}
